Compilation flags:
========================================
Enable : MODEL=HYDRO, EOS=ISOTHERMAL
Disable: COMOVING, PARTICLE, GRAVITY


Default setup:
========================================
1. Code units:
   (1) Dimensionless OPT__UNIT=0
   (2) Magnetic field is scaled to MagZ=Turb_B0/UNIT_B -> initial magnetic energy density = 0.5*Turb_B0^2/(4*pi)
   (3) Adjust MOLECULAR_WEIGHT and ISO_TEMP so Cs=1

2. BOX_SIZE         1
   NX0_TOT_X        64
   NX0_TOT_Y        64
   NX0_TOT_Z        64

3. MAX_LEVEL        0
   OPT__BC_FLU_*    1  (periodic)

4. END_T            default to 100 code unit

5. Turbulence parameters:
   SRC_TURBULENCE    1    enable turbulence
   TURB_VEL          0.2  target velocity dispersion in code unit
   TURB_KDRIV        2.0  driving scale, this will affect Ornstein-Uhlenbeck auto-correlation time (turnover time): Tdecay = BOX_SIZE/(TURB_VEL*TURB_KDRIV)
   TURB_KMIN         1.0  minimum wave number in units of 2*pi/BOX_SIZE
   TURB_KMAX         3.0  maximum wave number in units of 2*pi/BOX_SIZE
   TURB_ZETA         1.0  fully solenoidal
   TURB_SPEC_FORM    1    parabolic spectrum
   TURB_UPDATE_STEP  10   number of turbulence driving pattern updates per turnover time, so dt for OU process = Tdecay/TURB_UPDATE_STEP
   TURB_TABLE_SIZE   128  resolution of turbulence table, actual table size is (TURB_TABLE_SIZE + 1)^3

Reference:
========================================
1. Turbulence Generator: paper:       Federrath et al. (2010), A&A 512, A81 (https://doi.org/10.1051/0004-6361/200912437)
                         source code: TurbGen (https://github.com/chfeder/turbulence_generator)

2. Test problem inspired by Pakmor et al. (2026) (arXiv:2607.06660)

